44119 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 44120 0 R/Alt(Path diagram in black and white. SMA information and NCM information, on the left, each point to the evidence-relevance and evidence-incrimination factors, two ovals, which point to abortion likelihood, which points to the probable-cause ruling (probit) on the right; foreseeability, below, points to the ruling. The four outcome-information paths carry one value per record (stereotypical, non-stereotypical), the factor's intercept; the factor-to-likelihood and likelihood-to-ruling paths one value; the foreseeability path one value per outcome condition, tagged None, SMA and NCM. Each carries its unstandardized estimate and robust Wald 95% interval; a solid path marks an interval that excludes zero and a dashed path one that includes it.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[4]/Pg 48739 0 R>>
endobj
